Z||000025||theogre||04-12-2001||08:09 PM||||This was reported on one of the major news feeds today...<P>You can also thank your state law makers and the EPA. One of the problems is all the diferant blends required to meet clean air laws. All these diferant blends make it more expensive to store and deliver.<P>Another is a potential shortage of MTBE which is made from equally expensive natural gas. (MTBE is an emission control additive.) As NG prices rose production of MTBE was reduced. <P>It is expected some areas could break over $3.00 per gallon this summer. Many areas could see record prices as soon as May.<P>||||reg||1
